WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.480
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:15.890
Last time: AND · OR · NOT

3
00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:21.960
Chapter 3 · Sorting and Comparing

4
00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:30.160
Bigger? Smaller? In order?

5
00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:36.570
Meet Aarav and Zara, marble fans!

6
00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:44.320
Aarav: 36 marbles · Zara: 63 marbles

7
00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:54.640
36 or 63. Who has more? Think!

8
00:00:54.640 --> 00:01:07.880
63 = 6 tens · 36 = 3 tens → 63 is bigger

9
00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:15.210
Comparing: bigger, smaller, or the same?

10
00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:19.920
Three comparing signs

11
00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:29.000
> greater than · 9 > 4

12
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:33.160
< less than · 3 < 8

13
00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:40.660
= equal · 7 = 7

14
00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:47.030
Meet Chompy the crocodile!

15
00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:55.130
The open mouth eats the bigger number

16
00:01:55.130 --> 00:02:03.860
15 > 12 · the mouth faces 15

17
00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:16.630
8 < 10 · the mouth faces 10

18
00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:23.320
Compare the biggest place first

19
00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:35.000
3 tens < 6 tens, so 36 < 63

20
00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:49.340
Same tens? Check ones: 45 < 48

21
00:02:49.340 --> 00:03:06.600
Same hundreds · 0 tens < 5 tens → 305 < 350

22
00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:25.310
Only one is true. Which one?

23
00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:36.320
15 > 12 is the true one!

24
00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:42.110
Sorting = putting things in order

25
00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:51.610
Toy car boxes: 12, 5, 30, 21, 9

26
00:03:51.610 --> 00:04:01.660
Find the smallest · write it · cross it out

27
00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:13.190
5 → 9 → 12 → 21 → 30

28
00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:23.600
Sorted! The biggest box has 30 cars

29
00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:41.940
Up: 8, 17, 25 · Down: 25, 17, 8

30
00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:58.170
Which list is biggest to smallest?

31
00:04:58.170 --> 00:05:10.370
50, 42, 31, 19, 6 · each one smaller

32
00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:21.810
14, 3, 27, 3. Two 3s! What now?

33
00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:33.950
Keep both: 3, 3, 14, 27

34
00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:48.760
Pencils: 9, 14, 6, 11, 8 cm. The middle one?

35
00:05:48.760 --> 00:06:00.220
6, 8, 9, 11, 14 · the middle is 9 cm

36
00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:06.590
Sorted lists are faster to search

37
00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:15.780
Messy list: check one by one… slow!

38
00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:26.390
Sorted list: jump near the end. Found!

39
00:06:26.390 --> 00:06:30.090
Your turn: practice check

40
00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:41.570
Sort 19, 7, 42, 7 (smallest first)

41
00:06:41.570 --> 00:06:49.030
7, 7, 19, 42 · both 7s stay!

42
00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:57.430
> greater · < less · = equal

43
00:06:57.430 --> 00:06:59.560
Compare the biggest place first

44
00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:04.340
Sort: smallest, then the next

45
00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:06.990
Sorted lists are faster to search

46
00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:12.720
Chapter 3 done!

47
00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:19.520
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
